# What `docker build .` must not send (master plan P9 task 3, added 2026-09-19).
#
# There was no .dockerignore until the first Windows build, so the build context was the
# whole checkout — including a Windows virtualenv that cannot run in a Linux image, every
# __pycache__, and .git. The Dockerfile COPYs only app/, migrations/, scripts/ and data/,
# so none of these reached the image; they only made every build ship them to the daemon.
#
# data/bm25/ is excluded, and that is a decision, not hygiene. Measured 2026-09-19 on the
# first image built on Windows: `COPY data ./data` put 25 third-party PDFs (462 MB) into
# the image, several with `z-library` in the filename — shadow-library copies of commercial
# books. A pushed image redistributes whatever it carries (CLAUDE.md "Known landmines"
# item 1). Excluding is the reversible direction — delete this line to ship them — and
# shipping is not, so the default is out. The derived index goes too: it is untracked, so
# no CI build has it anyway, and it holds the books' text. `search_documentation` is gated
# on the index existing, so the tool is simply not offered — honest degradation, nothing
# half-works. data/verify/ stays: the trust page publishes from it.
data/bm25/

.git
.gitignore
venv/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.env
.env.local
*.log
node_modules/
tests/
docs/
